From 5abc650eec157d2a762c82161589a2be1c0f7607 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:18:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 005/197] Core: run a script piped into FreeCADCmd as one
 script

'FreeCADCmd < script.py' fed the input line by line to the interactive
console: prompts and the banner were mixed into the output, a blank line
was required after every block, and errors ended with exit code 0.
When stdin is not a terminal and no file is given, compile the whole
input as '<stdin>' and run it in __main__ like the Python executable
does, with sys.argv == ['-', ...] and a non-zero exit code on errors.
Interactive use from a terminal is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/App/Application.cpp | 74 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 64 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

